**[Suggestion]** The `available` width calculation reads `header.clientWidth` but never subtracts the width of the optional workspace-tag sibling (`.workspaceTag`, `flex: 0 1 auto`, `max-width: 50%`) that appears before the title in the `.header` flex container on multi-workspace panes. Additionally, `headerGap = 8` subtracts one inter-child gap, but the header has 2 gaps when the workspace tag is visible (workspaceTag → title → PaneHeaderActions = 3 children, 2 gaps = 16 px).

**Failure scenario:** In a multi-workspace daemon with split panes, the workspace tag consumes 50–120 px (dot + name + padding) plus an 8 px flex gap. `available` is overestimated by that amount, so host actions stay inline when they should collapse. The title (`flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0`) gets crushed below the intended 64 px `TITLE_MIN_WIDTH_PX` minimum before `measure.scrollWidth > available` finally flips true.

```suggestion
 const workspaceTag = header.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-web-shell-pane-workspace]`);
 const workspaceTagWidth = workspaceTag?.offsetWidth ?? 0;
 const workspaceTagGap = workspaceTagWidth > 0 ? headerGap : 0;
 const available =
 header.clientWidth -
 padding -
 workspaceTagWidth -
 workspaceTagGap -
 TITLE_MIN_WIDTH_PX -
 trailingWidth -
 headerGap -
 actionsGap;
 setCollapsed(measure.scrollWidth > available);
```

